<title>BELGIUM: Kredietbank H1 1996 net profit up 14.5%.</title>
<headline>Kredietbank H1 1996 net profit up 14.5%.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996 (in billions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			  6.69  vs  5.84</p>
<p>Cons net interest income(up 13.4%) 27.59  vs 24.32</p>
<p>    Other Income (up 56.3%)		12.56  vs  8.04</p>
<p>    -of which exchange,trading income   3.68  vs  0.95</p>
<p>NOTE - Kredietbank NV is one of Belgium's four largest banks.  </p>
<p>-of which other commission income  6.47  vs  4.67</p>
<p>    Cons current gross income	   40.15  vs 32.36</p>
<p>    Operating costs			 21.49  vs 19.73</p>
<p>Cons operating results(up47.8 pct)18.66  vs 12.62</p>
<p>Depreciations,write downs,</p>
<p>    provisions (up 90.1 pct)	     7.87  vs  4.14</p>
<p>    Extraordinary gains		    0.14  vs  0.09</p>
<p>    Cons pretax profit(up 27.4 pct)   10.92  vs  8.57</p>
<p>    Income taxes			     3.99  vs  2.46</p>
<p>    Cons net profit			  7.02  vs  6.15</p>
<p>    Cons total assets		   3,509.6  vs 2,961.5</p>
<p>Customer deposits and debts</p>
<p>    represented by securities	 1,841.5  vs 1,560.1</p>
<p>    Capital and reserves		   94.4  vs    86.0</p>
<p>    Risk Asset Ratio(in percent)*	10.7  vs    11.3</p>
<p>    -of which core capital(in percent)* 5.7  vs     5.9</p>
<p>NOTE-*calculated according to Banking and Finance Commission decision of December 5, 1995: Capital Adequacy Directive.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
